{
  "schema": 1,
  "note": "THE CARRY FAMILY'S CELLS, AS DATA. One record per cell; tests, tools/probe_cells.py and the benches read this file instead of each keeping their own copy. Started at C1c; G5 completes the consolidation (it retires tools/probe_cells.py's frozen mirror and the benches' inline specs). A record is a DECLARATION of a draw and a shape, never of an arm: the arm key is (D, DV, warps_per_cta) and is derived from `widths`, `dv` and `warps_per_cta` by rola.ops.carry.",
  "fields": {
    "name": "the cell's identity; a seed is derived from it (crc32) so a failure reproduces from its own name",
    "widths": "the descriptor's PADDED per-level digit counts B_l (powers of two at or above 16)",
    "dv": "the descriptor's PADDED value width DV, one of rola.ops.carry.SHIPPED_DV",
    "tokens": "L, the sequence length in tokens; any L is lawful (the kernel runs a partial window)",
    "warps_per_cta": "the launch shape; 8 is shipped, 4 is the two-CTA latency diagnostic",
    "draw": "dense | alt | both | cohort -- which support structure the routing is drawn with",
    "k_tok": "nonzeros per row per sparse level; a property of the DRAW and never told to the kernel",
    "cohort": "for draw=cohort, the run of consecutive tokens sharing one contiguous digit window",
    "support": "the leading fraction of each level's digits the draw may use (structured truncation)",
    "backing": "dense | paged -- which state backing the cell binds",
    "state": "none | fresh | carried -- whether the cell binds an entry state and chains",
    "tier": "oracle | probe | both -- who reads this record"
  },
